course: dictionary
lesson: 5985
title: Meadows: fields of grass and flowers
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A meadow is a field of grass and wild flowers. Animals can graze on it, and farmers sometimes cut its grass to make hay. Meadows are often peaceful places for picnics and play.
explain: Look at the words around the word. «Suddenly he throws down his brush and digs his way up into the sunshine of a big meadow.» Digging up into sunshine tells you the meadow is a place out in the open, with grass and light. What word would fit here? A field of grass fits.
explain: Some words are built from smaller words. Meadow-grass is grass that grows in a meadow, and meadow-sweet is a plant that grows there too. When you spot the small word inside a bigger one, the meaning often becomes clear.
fact: A meadow is a field of grass and wild flowers.
fact: «A wildflower meadow» is a meadow full of wild flowers.
fact: Meadows are homes for bees, butterflies, grasshoppers and field mice.
fact: «Marmots» are big ground squirrels that live on mountain meadows.
fact: Wildflower meadows help pollinators, such as bees, to find food.
exercise: «Suddenly he throws down his brush and digs his way up into the sunshine of a big meadow.» Where is he? | Inside a classroom | In a dark cellar under a house | Under the sea | *In a big field of grass and flowers
exercise: «A girl in Montana on a family hike sees a black bear across a meadow.» What does across a meadow mean? | Down a deep hole | Inside a small wooden hut | *Over the grass and flowers, from one side to the other | Under a heavy bridge
exercise: Sam says a meadow is a kind of busy road. What is a meadow really? | A small pond with fish | *A field of grass and wild flowers | A busy road with cars | A tall building in a town
test: «Marmots are big ground squirrels of mountain meadows.» Where do marmots live? | In shops and offices | *On mountain meadows | Inside the sea | In tall city buildings
test: What is a wildflower meadow full of? | Bricks and glass | *Wild flowers | Sand and rocks | Cars and roads
exam: Why are meadows good places for bees and butterflies? | They are full of concrete and shops | They have deep water and sharks | *They have flowers and food for them to eat | They are always covered in snow
